# Configuration for GPU Fan Control
# BareCortex

# Target fan speed percentage (0-100), written by `bmc-fan --percent`.
# The write is per device and the service reports the driver's answer, so a
# card that ignores manual fan control fails the start instead of passing it.
FAN_SPEED="80"

# Log file location. One line per start and stop, recording bmc-fan's exit
# status; the per-device detail goes to the service's own output.
LOG_FILE="/var/log/gpu-fancontrol.log"

# There is no interval or fan-curve setting here. A polling policy needs the
# threshold source, the interval and the safe state on a failed read, and those
# are gpu-stack 7.1-7.3's to decide. The previous file carried a CHECK_INTERVAL
# that nothing in the service read.
